## Red-Proof A — passphrase leak in approval-client (Invariant I1)

1. Condition asserted: `approval-client.ts` never touches browser
   storage; `approval-invariant.test.ts` static probe
   (`touchesStorage(code) === false`) plus runtime sign path must hold.
2. Sabotage (minimal, targeted): inserted one line into
   `approveWithSecret` in `web/src/security/approval-client.ts`,
   immediately after `const keypair = deriveKeypairPem(secret);`:
   `localStorage.setItem("approval-passphrase", secret);`
3. Check run: `bun test web/test/approval-invariant.test.ts`
   → exit 1 (FAIL, as required — non-vacuous):
   `6 pass, 3 fail, 37 expect() calls`. Failing assertions:
   - `(fail) invariant I1 (static source discipline) > approval-client
     zeroes the closure secret and touches no storage`
     (`expect(touchesStorage(code)).toBe(false)` → received true).
   - Runtime sign tests threw `ReferenceError: localStorage is not
     defined` at the planted line (proving the leak path executes).
4. Revert: `git checkout -- web/src/security/approval-client.ts`
   → `RESTORED A`.
5. Clean check: `git status --short -- web/` → empty (clean).
6. Restore proof: `bun test web/test/approval-invariant.test.ts`
   → exit 0, `9 pass, 0 fail, 51 expect() calls`.

